<Section collapsed="true" isCollapsible="true" drawButton="true" MultipleChoiceAnswerIndex="-1" MultipleChoiceRandomizeChoices="false" TrueFalseAnswerIndex="-1" EssayAnswerRows="5" EssayAnswerColumns="60"><Title><Text-field style="Heading 1" layout="Heading 1">Question 5 Lecture 8</Text-field></Title>
<Group labelreference="L799" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field style="Normal" layout="Normal">Use <Font style="Text" bold="true">implicitplot3d</Font> to graph the 6 surfaces  in three space with equations given by <Equation executable="false" style="Normal" input-equation="" display=""></Equation> where  a is 1 or -1 and b is 0, 1 or -1. Make a title for each using the option</Text-field><Text-field style="Normal" layout="Normal">         <Font style="Text" bold="true">title=covert(x^2+a*y^2+b*z^2=1, string) </Font></Text-field><Text-field style="Normal" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Normal" layout="Normal">with the appropriate value of a and b inserted. Use also the option <Font style="Text" bold="true">axes=boxed</Font>. <Font style="Text" bold="true">You can <Font underline="true">and should</Font> do all 6 with a pair of do loops.</Font> And don't forget to shrink each plot before printing. You may need to use <Font style="Text" bold="true">print(display(...)) </Font>to get display to work properly inside two do loops.  </Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"></Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
